 HISTORY                                                          8010 1451
 -------                                                          8010 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics  8010 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The        8010 1451
 thermal scattering law data for uranium metal was developed      8010 1451
 using molecular dynamics (MD) with lattice dynamics [1]. The     8010 1451
 coherent elastic cross sections were calculated based on the     8010 1451
 experimental lattice constants. Free atom cross sections were    8010 1451
 taken from ENDF/B-VIII.0 nuclide evaluations at 1e-5 eV [2].     8010 1451
 Seven temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law   8010 1451
 Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to       8010 1451
 produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data for U-metal [3]. The coherent      8010 1451
 elastic data were prepared using the cubic approximation.        8010 1451
 MAT=8010 and ZA=8110 are used for U-metal (10% enriched).        8010 1451
